      "annotations": [
        {
          "id": "fGkfdoFP3MdY",
          "title": "Purpose",
          "lead": "Abraham Lincoln was the first president to use the new art of photography for political purposes. Photographs, paintings, and sculptures of him were created both before and during his presidency. By 1865, Lincoln was one of the most well-known figures in the country. Why do you think he took the time for this mask to be made?",
          "marker": "1",
          "articleId": "h1PS19XrvIQH",
          "style": "Circle",
          "position": [
            75.4042445,
            36.4496509,
            -39.319053
          ],
          "direction": [
            0.9073767,
            0.4045879,
            0.1139131
          ],
          "color": [
            0,
            0.61,
            0.87
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "1kfasSfNJ5ZA",
          "title": "Clark Mills",
          "lead": "Sculptor Clark Mills created this mask of Lincoln using a process he developed that involved greasing Lincoln’s whiskers.",
          "marker": "2",
          "articleId": "lTe3ea2rT3lj",
          "style": "Circle",
          "position": [
            56.0302351,
            -75.9206743,
            98.2365821
          ],
          "direction": [
            0.8425544,
            0.3566161,
            0.4036423
          ],
          "color": [
            0,
            0.61,
            0.87
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ImL9UR2vWarg",
          "title": "Age",
          "lead": "Do you think this is a representation of Lincoln at the beginning or end of the Civil War? Why do you think so?",
          "marker": "3",
          "style": "Circle",
          "position": [
            45.058907,
            -21.2213963,
            77.5726515
          ],
          "direction": [
            0.6471683,
            0.2078783,
            0.7334574
          ],
          "color": [
            0,
            0.61,
            0.87
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "fgfNL4pe3hAx",
          "title": "The Civil War",
          "lead": "As Lincoln looks out, frozen in time with hollowed cheeks and every line and wrinkle on his face recorded, we cannot help but think about the enormity of the challenge he had faced and was facing. When you look at Lincoln’s life mask, what visual clues illustrate his burdens, challenges, and successes?",
          "marker": "4",
          "articleId": "flqz1ooKNc3v",
          "style": "Circle",
          "position": [
            55.9756687,
            30.4978488,
            34.0021254
          ],
          "direction": [
            0.9294426,
            0.3417797,
            0.1390076
          ],
          "color": [
            0,
            0.61,
            0.87
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "E6afxomim99I",
          "title": "The Mind behind the Mask",
          "lead": "Lincoln’s life mask offers a window into his thoughts approximately two months before his assassination. Given what you know about Lincoln, what could he be thinking about as this mask was being created?",
          "marker": "5",
          "articleId": "y4cgikdMZ6JM",
          "style": "Circle",
          "position": [
            52.0298218,
            60.4820882,
            -6.4760381
          ],
          "direction": [
            0.6727749,
            0.7121184,
            0.2006521
          ],
          "color": [
            0,
            0.61,
            0.87
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tUO2nAVlgpvQ",
          "title": "Lincoln's Profile",
          "lead": "Examine the mask by comparing the left and right profiles. What similarities and differences do you see?",
          "marker": "6",
          "style": "Circle",
          "position": [
            -0.0727909,
            57.7410562,
            43.1754358
          ],
          "direction": [
            0.0117798,
            0.726418,
            0.6871522
          ],
          "color": [
            0,
            0.61,
            0.87
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "qmMMuGvfI9vp",
          "title": "Lincoln's Appearance",
          "lead": "After the start of the Civil War, Lincoln made a conscious choice to change his appearance. Compare the 1865 mask with the 1860 mask. What did he change and why?",
          "marker": "7",
          "articleId": "GKrrNdk5clEi",
